  m_Name: 1970 smoking
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  title: Smoking Bans in Public 1970s
  info: Smoking in public spaces like buses, MRT stations, hawker centers, and parks
    has been banned to protect public health. Over time, the ban expanded to beaches
    and recreational areas. Smoking is allowed only in designated smoking areas,
    and violations result in fines of up to SGD 1,000. The government also encourages
    smokers to quit through public awareness campaigns and accessible cessation programs,
    further promoting a smoke-free environment.
  image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 601d3872cb0a44da8847a6ead025f1aa, type: 3}
